mediatek/filogic: use UTF-8 for FAT filenames by default

block-mount mounts hotplugged partitions without any charset option, and the
kernel default for FAT is iocharset=iso8859-1 with FAT_DEFAULT_UTF8 unset, so
non-ASCII (e.g. Chinese) filenames on FAT32 sticks show up garbled. Enable
FAT_DEFAULT_UTF8 so vfat mounts behave like the exfat and ntfs3 drivers, which
already default to UTF-8. The symbol is not exposed through Config-kernel.in,
hence a target config patch instead of a CONFIG_KERNEL_* line.

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
@@ -169,6 +169,7 @@
 CONFIG_EXCLUSIVE_SYSTEM_RAM=y
 CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y
 CONFIG_F2FS_FS=y
+CONFIG_FAT_DEFAULT_UTF8=y
 CONFIG_FIXED_PHY=y
 CONFIG_FIX_EARLYCON_MEM=y
 CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER=y
